{"question":"What causal mechanisms remain credible for Harness v2 attempt 4 after inspecting the champion, corpus, code, and experiment ledger?","findings":"Read-only inspection confirms that the current path still offers only raw plus one canonical retrieval variant, collapses variant provenance before RRF, and makes a binary MATCHED/NOT_FOUND decision. I also verified the supplied label artifact contains 90 keyed labels despite the supervisor digest reporting zero parsed labels; excluding those keys and the 33 provisional rows reconstructs the intended 130-row review set.","decision_impact":"The nearby alternate-query/fusion/decomposition family is now empirically saturated. Remaining value is more plausibly in explicitly representing catalog-scope/evidence insufficiency, but corpus-ingestion consistency must be resolved before using the digest’s 220-row derived pool for class prevalence.","unresolved":"Whether scope/uncertainty changes improve user utility rather than merely recategorizing outcomes; no end-to-end labels exist for the unresolved pool.","sources":[],"evidence_patterns":[],"candidate_directions":[]}
